<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="causes"><span aria-hidden="true">01</span>Common reasons a computer becomes slow</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Microsoft lists several possible contributors to poor Windows PC performance, including low available storage, too many startup apps, outdated software and older hardware. Simple first checks can include closing apps you are not using, restarting the computer, reviewing available storage and checking which programs start automatically.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">These checks are useful clues, not a complete diagnosis. A computer may have more than one issue, and a change that helps one symptom may not solve another. Use Microsoft’s guidance as a starting point:</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted"><a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/experience/performance-optimization/tips-to-improve-pc-performance-in-windows">Microsoft’s Windows performance guidance</a></p>
{% call note("care", "Take care", "Skip the risky quick fixes") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Avoid risky “quick fixes” such as registry cleaners, deleting files you do not understand, or disabling security protections. If support or compatibility is relevant, check the current position rather than relying on an old article or assumption.</p>{% endcall %}
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="options"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span>Fix, upgrade or replace?</h2>
<p class="ed-section-intro">Three possible routes. None is an automatic verdict.</p>
<div class="ed-decisions">
{{ decision('fix', 'Fix', 'The computer is generally reliable but has one annoying symptom', 'Can the cause be identified and fixed safely within the existing setup?') }}
{{ decision('upgrade', 'Upgrade', 'It is usable but struggles with current everyday tasks', 'Would a suitable upgrade provide worthwhile improvement?') }}
{{ decision('replace', 'Replace', 'It is very old, unreliable or incompatible with required software', 'Would replacement be more practical than continued repairs?') }}
</div>
{% call note("care", "Take care", "Protect what matters first") %}<p>The problem involves important files, accounts or uncertain hardware condition. What needs to be protected or assessed before making changes?</p>{% endcall %}
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">The right answer depends on the computer, the fault, the software you use and the value of your time. Compare the total quoted cost of the work with the cost of a suitable replacement, including setup and moving your files. Ask what the proposed change is expected to improve and what it will leave unresolved.</p><blockquote class="ed-pullquote">There is no single birthday at which every computer must be replaced.</blockquote>
{% call note("info", "Good to know", "Compare the whole cost") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">A cheap part is not automatically a good investment if the rest of the system is near the end of its useful life. Conversely, replacement may be unnecessary when a straightforward, safe adjustment solves the actual problem.</p>{% endcall %}
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">If the delay happens when switching on or signing in, read our <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="/guides/computer-slow-startup/">guide to a computer that takes a long time to start</a>.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">If the delay is mainly online, our <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="/guides/slow-computer-or-internet/">computer or internet comparison guide</a> helps you describe where the waiting starts.</p>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="try"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span>If you only have ten minutes</h2>
{% call note("info", "Try this · ten minutes", "Describe one real task") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Start by describing one real task that feels slow: opening email, joining a video call or finding a document. Note whether the delay happens before the computer is ready, inside one program or only when using the internet. Those are different starting points for a conversation, even when the experience feels equally frustrating.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">The useful outcome is a clear next step. You should be able to understand what was checked, what was changed, what remains uncertain and whether more work would need a separate quote.</p>
{% endcall %}
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="checklist"><span aria-hidden="true">04</span>A practical checklist</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Before arranging help, note what you can. You do not need to answer every question or diagnose the computer yourself:</p>
<ul class="ed-checklist"><li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>When did the slowdown begin?</span></label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Is it present at startup, while opening programs, or during a particular task?</span></label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Does restarting make a temporary difference?</span></label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>How much storage appears to be available?</span></label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Which programs do you use most often?</span></label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Has the computer shown unusual messages, crashes or hardware noise?</span></label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Are there important files or accounts that need special care?</span></label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Do you need the computer for work, study, communication or another time-sensitive purpose?</span></label></li></ul><p class="ed-caption">Use the ticks as a reading aid. They are not saved or sent anywhere.</p>
